## CROSS-CUTTING — Category I: Integration Between Security & Alerts

**35. Security findings should be able to generate alert RULES, not just display data.**
A Security finding ("3 users without MFA") is currently a passive observation. It should offer: "Create alert rule: MFA_GAP > threshold → fire SECURITY/HIGH." One click generates the ALERT_CONFIG INSERT.

*Reasoning:* Security posture findings that don't become monitored rules are one-time observations. Turning them into rules creates persistent governance — the system alerts when posture degrades again.

**36. The Security "Exposure" inventory should fire alerts when a new LISTING share appears.**
Shares are the data exposure surface. A new marketplace listing appearing should fire an alert: "NEW_LISTING_SHARE — a share was published to the marketplace; verify authorization." Currently this is visible only when someone opens the Exposure section.

*Reasoning:* A new listing could be unauthorized data sharing. Passive visibility isn't enough; proactive alerting catches it in hours, not weeks.

**37. Alert resolution notes should be searchable and linked to Security investigations.**
When an alert is resolved with kind=ACTIONED and a note like "Disabled user JSMITH — compromised credential confirmed," that resolution is security-relevant evidence. Surface it on the Security page under the relevant user's Entity 360.

*Reasoning:* Alert resolution notes are institutional memory. Currently they exist only in ALERT_AUDIT — not connected to the entity they describe. Cross-linking creates a complete investigation record.

